		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=820#comment-8518</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[A Memory of Poul Ove Pedersen.

The way Poul died was in complete accordance with some of his positive qualities, such as full acceptance of how things were in life, a humility and gratefulness for all that life had given him. Thus he felt no fear, only completion and confidence in what was to come, whatever it was. His only wish was to die in the presence of his wife, Nini Leick, and so he did, in his home. To those of us who were present during his last week, Poul serves as a model for dying in dignity and serenity.]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>A Memory of Poul Ove Pedersen.</p>
<p>The way Poul died was in complete accordance with some of his positive qualities, such as full acceptance of how things were in life, a humility and gratefulness for all that life had given him. Thus he felt no fear, only completion and confidence in what was to come, whatever it was. His only wish was to die in the presence of his wife, Nini Leick, and so he did, in his home. To those of us who were present during his last week, Poul serves as a model for dying in dignity and serenity.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
